Z||000000||2birds||12-12-1999||10:22 PM||||I have a strange thing happening with my steering wheel.  It is a stock 86 GT wheel, and there is a brown semi-liquid substance oozing out from between the stitching.  It is the consistency of a melted Hershey bar.  This started when I first moved down to the Southeast US.  The leather is also really loose and saggy on the wheel now.  I really like the shape and feel of the stock wheel, so I am interested in getting it repaired and recovered (the thumbrests are starting to wear through now).  Anyone know of a good shop to do this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||12-12-1999||10:36 PM||||The Fiero Store sells reconditioned GT steering wheels for $189 and a $189 core charge!!!! I think I would consider an aftermarket steering wheel.<P>Okay- I got out my Fiero Store catalog and the steering wheel is part #75000 at $189.00 and the core charge is listed as #75002 at $189.00- as if it mattered!<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 12-13-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-12-1999||11:35 PM||||I was in the same boat, my 85 GT steering wheel was in sad shape, but I didn't really want to spend almost $200 for a reconditioned one. I posted a want ad in the mall and a Forum member sold me a good one for a reasonable price.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-13-1999||12:10 AM||||It's a $100 core charge, but I've gotta agree.  Buy a different one.  You can get a real nice aftermarket one for less than the core charge.  But keep that one in your attic.  Someday, someone will want one to have restored and maybe you can make some $$.  (Of course, I don't throw anything "Fiero" away!)||||reg||1
Z||000004||dogtired||12-13-1999||11:04 AM||||Had the exact same thing on my 86GT, just thought the previous owner was a slob  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Well he was a slob, but that didn't have anything to do with the steering wheel. I think it is the padding/foam breaking down. Guess I will call the Fiero Store the way I read the add for a wheel was *$189.  then the *$100. core charge, therefore I though after you sent your old wheel in, the end cost was $89.???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Has anyone asked them or ordered a wheel??||||reg||6
Z||000005||Shiner||12-13-1999||11:10 AM||||My wheel is absolutly HORRIBLE.  The leather is actually MISSING in alot of places!  That disgusting brown goop is under all of it too. I absolutly HATE those cheap aftermarket wheels (like Grant, no offense guys, I just like stock better), and Momo wheels are WAY too expensive for me right now.  How does the Fiero Store wheel look?  I know Mr. Mike does them, for $175 (in any color you want), no core charge, and he even gives you a loaner. Nice deal, but a little too expensive for me.||||reg||5
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-13-1999||02:17 PM||||I think the total cost of the Fiero Store restoration is $189 (plus tax and shipping, I'm sure).  The core charge is in addition to the restoration charge.  And the steering wheel you send in must be good.  Not the covering, but don't try to send them one that is bent.  They have to be able to use that for the next customer.<P>BTW, Shiner--Grant doesn't just make those old cheap, generic wheel anymore.  The have wheel that rival some of the VERY expensive brands such as Momo.  You should check out their catalog sometime.  Try an auto parts store.  Wal-mart only carries the cheap, generic ones.  <p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-13-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-13-1999||08:48 PM||||The sport steering wheel, the one with the paddle horn buttons, 4 heavy round spokes, and the soft rim, is use in a number of other GM cars. The only diferance is the center trim between the horn buttons which is changable. The wheel is available with gray or black hand rim.<P>That wheel might not be as pretty but it's the least fatiging of the bunch on a long trip. And it's a stock fiero item.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||12-13-1999||11:04 PM||||My car ('86 SC) has a similar wheel but it has the round horn button in the middle.  I like it better than the one with the 2 horn paddles.  Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000009||AL||12-14-1999||01:18 AM||||you know guys if you want a steering wheel you can go to the junkyard and take one off a firebird, they have the same steering wheel.just a thought, plus it's cheaper and there are alot of firebirds out there.||||reg||1
Z||000010||2birds||12-14-1999||09:02 PM||||Thanks for the input.  My wheel is the leather three spoke design with the thumbrests, and I've really gotten used to it after 11 years.  I've looked at some of the Grant designs, but the leather ones aren't much less than the Fiero Store's resto price.  I've heard some good things about Mr. Mike's interior work.  Anyone know if he's online?<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 12-14-1999).]||||reg||1
